    {
      "id": "05-01",
      "title": "Which route should this packet take?",
      "chapter": "The routing puzzle",
      "duration": 21.6,
      "narration": "A packet at router A needs to reach router F. Several paths exist, but the path with fewer links is not necessarily the cheapest. Watch the colored packet choose between alternatives. By the end, you will calculate its route and explain how routers learn enough information to make that choice.",
      "bullets": [
        "One destination, several paths",
        "Best depends on the metric"
      ],
      "takeaway": "A route is best only relative to its chosen metric.",
