      "title": "Install the next hop",
      "chapter": "From algorithm to routers",
      "duration": 21.6,
      "narration": "Router A does not need to attach the whole drawn path to every packet. For destination F, this calculation selects C as the next hop. C makes its own forwarding choice when the packet arrives. Real forwarding entries typically describe destination prefixes, so one entry can cover many destination addresses.",
      "bullets": [
        "Destination F: next hop C",
        "Real routes usually identify prefixes"
