      "duration": 22.033333333333335,
      "narration": "Split horizon avoids advertising a learned route back toward the neighbor from which it was learned. Poisoned reverse explicitly advertises that reverse direction as unreachable. Triggered updates can spread changes sooner. These techniques help, but do not turn a basic distance-vector protocol into an instant, universally loop-free solution for every topology.",
